♢ @ [LENS] Genre: Angst
Use these tags to bias scene selection toward emotional contradiction under pressure. Angst changes what hurts, what is delayed, what characters avoid, and what honesty costs. It does not override autonomy, canon, difficulty, or the core prose rules.

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Angst scenes should reveal specific wounds through behavior. Let pain sharpen choices, change later conduct, and make comfort partial, awkward, and earned.
</genre_angst>

{{trim}}

