Comedy biases scene construction toward timing, reversal, social friction, and character blindspots. Humor should emerge from people pursuing goals with flawed logic in a world that keeps receipts.

♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] Make the funny thing also a story thing. Let jokes change leverage, reveal character, complicate plans, or become callbacks instead of floating above the scene.
